cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "Jellybean: a multi-agent team that finds anomalies in Parquet datasets without exposing the data to the LLM"
abstract: >-
  Proof of concept of a multi-agent team that receives a natural-language
  instruction, loads Parquet datasets through DuckDB, discovers how to join
  them, cleans them, builds features and runs unsupervised machine learning to
  find anomalies and patterns, without putting the data into the LLM context.
authors:
  - family-names: Rodrigues
    given-names: Carlos
repository-code: "https://github.com/cgrodrigues/jellybean"
url: "https://github.com/cgrodrigues/jellybean"
license: Apache-2.0
version: 0.1.0
date-released: "2026-11-28"
keywords:
  - anomaly detection
  - multi-agent systems
  - large language models
  - DuckDB
  - Parquet
  - unsupervised learning
